 null, 'An isometric contraction generates tension without any change in muscle length, as when pushing against an immovable object.'),
('NEET PG', 'Pre- and Para-Clinical Sciences', 'Physiology', 'medium', 'mcq',
 'The Frank-Starling law of the heart states that:',
 '[{"text":"Heart rate always remains constant regardless of venous return","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Increased venous return (preload) increases the force of cardiac contraction","isCorrect":true},{"text":"Cardiac output is independent of venous return","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Decreased preload always increases stroke volume","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb,
 null, 'The Frank-Starling law states that, within physiological limits, an increase in venous return (and hence ventricular filling/preload) leads to a stronger contraction and increased stroke volume.'),
('NEET PG', 'Pre- and Para-Clinical Sciences', 'Physiology', 'medium', 'mcq',
