 null, 'The Philadelphia chromosome, resulting from a t(9;22) translocation forming the BCR-ABL fusion gene, is the hallmark genetic abnormality of chronic myeloid leukemia.'),
('NEET PG', 'Pre- and Para-Clinical Sciences', 'Pathology', 'medium', 'mcq',
 'Unlike apoptosis, necrosis is characterized by:',
 '[{"text":"Cell shrinkage with no inflammatory response","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Cell swelling, membrane rupture, and an inflammatory response","isCorrect":true},{"text":"Orderly DNA fragmentation with no membrane damage","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Complete absence of any cellular changes","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb,
 null, 'Necrosis involves cell swelling, membrane rupture, and spillage of cellular contents that triggers inflammation, in contrast to the orderly, non-inflammatory process of apoptosis.'),

